417 - O Solemn Thought
 / 
Key: D
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 417
Topic: Doctrines - 

Verse 1:
[D]O solemn thought and can it [A7/C#]be
[A7/C#]The [D7/C]hour o [Bm]judgment now [A7/C#]is [D]come
[D]Which soon must fix our destiny,
[A7/C#]And [D7/C]seal the [Bm]sinner's fearful [F#7/A#]down?
[F#m]Yes, it is [Bm]so; [A]the [G]judgment [Em]hour
[G/D]Is swiftly [A7/C#]hastening [Bm]to its [F#/A#]close;
[F#]Then will [A]the Judge, [Bm]in [A]mighty [G]power,
[G/D]Descend [A7/C#]in [D]vengeance [G]on [A7]His [D]foes.

Verse 2:
[D]He who came down to earth to [A7/C#]die
[A7/C#]An offering [Bm]for the sins [A7/C#]of [D]men,
[D]And then ascended upon on [A7/C#]high,
[A7/C#]And [D7/C]will e'er [Bm]long return [Em/B]again,
[F#m]Is standing [Bm]now [A]before [G]the [Em]ark,
[G/D]And [A/C#]mercy [D]seat [A/C#]and [Bm]cherubim,
[F#]To [A]plead His [Bm]blood [A]for [G]saints, and [Em]make
[G/D]The [A/C#]last [A7/C#]remembrance [G]of [A7]their [D]sin.

Verse 3:
[D]The solemn moment is at [A7/C#]hand
[A7/C#]When [D7/C]we who [Bm]have His name [A7/C#]confessed,
[D]Each in his lot must singly [A7/C#]stand
[A7/C#]And [D7/C]pass the [Bm]final, searching [F#7/A#]test.
[F#m]Jesus! we [Bm]hope [A]in [G]Thee alone;
[G/D]In [A/C#]mercy [D]now [A/C#]upon [Bm]us [F#/A#]look,
[F#]Confess [A]our names before [G]the [Em]throne,
[G/D]And [A/C#]blot [A7/C#]our [D]sins [F#m]fromout [A7]Thy [D]book.

Verse 4:
[D]O blessed Savior! may we feel
[A7/C#]The [D7/C]full importance [Bm]of [A7/C#]this [D]hour.
[D]Inspire our hearts with holy [A7/C#]zeal,
[A7/C#]And aid [D7/C]us by [Bm]Thy Spirit's [Em/B]power,
[F#m]That we may [Bm]in [A]Thy [G]strength be [Em]strong,
[G/D]And [A/C#]brave [A7/C#]the [D]conflict [Bm]valiantly;
[F#]Then, [A]on Mount [Bm]Zion, [A]join [G]the song,
[G/D]And swell [A/C#]the [A7/C#]notes [F#m]of [G]victory.
